<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed bin Rashid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-maktoum">Al Maktoum</a> is the ruler of Dubai and has been vice-president and prime minister of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> since 2006. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-saeed-al-maktoum">Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum</a>, he served as the federation's first defence minister from 1971 and drove Dubai's growth into a global hub of trade, aviation, tourism and finance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohammed-bin-rashid-al-maktoum.jpg" alt="Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: http://www.president.gov.ua/ · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mohammed_bin_Rashid_Al_Maktoum_(15-02-2021).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
